  "question": {
    "text": "Two waves are described by the equations:<br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\rAnd <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0.46</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>92</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\rHere&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> are in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.<br />\rFind the number of times <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> becomes zero per second, at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>46</mn></math>",
